@code{x} that can result from executing

@lisp
(define x 10)
(parallel-execute 
 (lambda () (set! x (* x x)))
 (lambda () (set! x (* x x x))))
@end lisp

Which of these possibilities remain if we instead use serialized procedures:

@lisp
(define x 10)
(define s (make-serializer))
(parallel-execute 
 (s (lambda () (set! x (* x x))))
